# [460-fork] Local backup-pull script — contains the server IP, root SSH
# target and internal Docker volume path. MUST NOT be committed to this
# public repo. The generic, secret-free runbook lives in
# docs/ours-backup-and-restore.md instead.
Backup Pull script/
460tp-backup-pull.ps1

# [460-fork] Generated user-guide .docx — build artefact. The markdown
# source of truth is docs/ours-user-guide.md; regenerate the .docx with
# "Backup Pull script/build-user-guide.cjs". Keeping the binary out of git
# avoids noisy diffs and merge conflicts on a rendered file. The PDF
# hand-out (exported from the .docx to send to companions) is the same kind
# of artefact, so it's ignored too.
460 Trip Planner - User Guide.docx
460 Trip Planner - User Guide.pdf
*.docx

# [460-fork] Local manual-test data — real trip photos + exported JSON used
# when exercising import/export and the journal by hand. Large binaries
# (hundreds of MB); never belongs in the repo. (Was swept in once by an
# accidental `git add -A`; ignored here so it cannot recur.)
/Testing/

# [460-fork] Package lockfiles are intentionally UNTRACKED. They were
# generated on Windows and lack Linux-platform optional deps (rollup/sharp
# bindings), so the Dockerfile and CI use `npm install`, not `npm ci`.
# Ignoring them by path enforces that decision and stops an accidental add
# from silently breaking the Linux build. Full rationale in ci.yml.
/client/package-lock.json
/server/package-lock.json

# [460-fork] Throwaway local diagnostic scripts (e.g. PWA-install probe).
/probe-install.mjs
